cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AeroWM-FDIR: latent world-model control with real-time fault detection, isolation and recovery for 6-DOF powered descent"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. The artefacts (benchmark results, telemetry figure and trained checkpoints) are released with the repository; see LIMITATIONS.md for the scope of the claims."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Shushant"
    given-names: "Shushant"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Shushant17711/AeroWM-FDIR"
url: "https://github.com/Shushant17711/AeroWM-FDIR"
abstract: >-
  AeroWM-FDIR is a research stack for powered descent of a 6-DOF vehicle in
  simulation. It combines a recurrent state-space latent world model
  (RSSM, TD-MPC2 heads), an exact one-step physics-residual fault detector
  with a 5-way isolator and latched class decision, a fault-conditioned
  classical control law with a bounded learned residual, and a latent MPPI
  planner. On the published 20-episode-per-mode benchmark the fault detector
  alarms 0.9 steps (18 ms) after onset with 100 % detection and 99-100 %
  isolation accuracy, and the FDIR stack lands 90-100 % of the faulted
  flights while a non-adaptive cascaded-PID reference lands 0-40 %.
keywords:
  - fault detection and isolation
  - world models
  - model predictive control
  - powered descent
  - 6-DOF rigid-body dynamics
  - reinforcement learning
